              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "an odd number.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{112}{221}$.\n\nAdd the odd–even and even–odd selection probabilities.",
          "worked": "There are 28 odd-valued cards and 24 even-valued cards. An odd sum requires one card of each parity. Let $O$ denote an odd-valued card and $E$ an even-valued card, in drawing order.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{odd sum})&=P(OE)+P(EO)\\\\P(\\text{odd sum})&=\\frac{28}{52}\\times\\frac{24}{51}+\\frac{24}{52}\\times\\frac{28}{51}\\\\P(\\text{odd sum})&=\\frac{112}{221}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q28-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p25-q28-b-prompt",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "an even number.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{109}{221}$.\n\nSubtract the odd-sum probability from 1.",
          "worked": "An even sum is the complementary event to an odd sum.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{even sum})&=1-\\frac{112}{221}\\\\P(\\text{even sum})&=\\frac{109}{221}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      }
